  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: cd96477d5695e8349a71dcd12e8bd8d2, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'My dear,


    Rosa here. You have come a long way, so I send you
    something from my heart: mole.


    In Oaxaca, a family''s mole is its signature.
    My grandmother''s had more than twenty ingredients, and she never wrote them
    down. I learned by standing next to her for years, tasting, failing, tasting
    again.


    Chili, chocolate, spices, toasted slowly, ground, and simmered for
    hours until dark and deep. Serve it over chicken.


    Some things can only
    be taught by standing beside someone. I hope these letters were a little like
    that.'
